From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: The named pipe channel binding (net.pipe).

WsCreateChannel and WsCreateListener returned E_NOTIMPL for WS_NAMEDPIPE_CHANNEL_BINDING.
A named pipe channel is a duplex session (as WCF's NetNamedPipeBinding) with the .NET message
framing a net.tcp session has, over a named pipe: the TCP session code, its bytes sent and
received through the socket or the pipe. A service is published and found as WCF's
are (pipe.c, the scheme from WCF's MIT-licensed sources): a named file mapping, its name from
the URL ('Global\' or 'Local\', 'net.pipe:E' and the base64 of net.pipe://+/PATH/, or
'net.pipe:H' and that of its SHA-256 for long names), holding the GUID that names the pipe;
a client tries the hosts +, its own and *, Global before Local, from its path up. The
listener keeps one waiting instance (local clients only) and gives each accepted client's
to its channel.
